    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a significant offensive spark today, led by **Kyle Tucker**, who commands the highest score of the day at 77.359. He draws a highly favorable matchup against Y. Marte (xERA 5.16), offering a substantial ceiling that makes him our primary target for production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** follows closely at 73.66, buoyed by a significant 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Pfaadt. While **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** face the same pitcher, both benefit from a 16% park factor uplift and a slow delivery from the opposition that enhances their stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our Roto standings where every bag counts.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involves the utility and bench spots. **Wade Meckler** barely clings to a starting role with a 40.23 score, saved primarily by his leadoff-adjacent spot in the order, despite a harsh -13% adjustment against the tough Joe Ryan. **Brayan Rocchio** was our closest bench candidate at 51.90, but he was ultimately relegated to the pine because his production profile did not provide the specific category density required to displace our current starters. We continue to monitor **Miguel Vargas**, who holds a strong 0.378 xwOBA but lacks the situational platoon leverage to overtake our infield core today. \n\nAs we approach first pitch, be aware that while the matchups appear favorable on paper, the volatility of the bottom-third of our lineup\u2014specifically **Wade Meckler** and **Nasim Nunez**\u2014requires close observation. We remain thin in depth as we navigate the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** on the IL. Ensure that any last-minute lineup changes for **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci** do not necessitate a shift in our strategy, as we need consistent at-bats to maintain our pace in the 5x5 chase.",
